  "sourceInterpretation": [
    "The diagnostic observed 14 other threads with constant class counts, managed TP workers changing 3 to 5 to 4, and SQLx workers changing 1 to 3. The two threads retaining the executable comm are not both assigned semantic roles from names alone.",
    "Each database source constructs one owner thread and two asynchronous Tokio workers, with maximum four additional blocking workers. Two SQLite sources therefore reserve at most eight additional configured blocking workers, distinct from SQLx physical-connection workers.",
    "SQLx 0.9 constructs a dedicated named worker for each SQLite connection. Configured physical connection capacities are 16 business and 2 consumer; native logical session counters do not count those physical workers.",
    "The Server uses one current-thread runtime while serving. Its separate close helper occurs during shutdown and shares a Linux-truncated comm prefix; a prospective monitor must distinguish the exact pre-closure stage boundary from final shutdown.",
    "This diagnostic does not reproduce 25 threads or identify the extra thread in the failed steady attempt. It cannot by itself prove the complete 30-minute resource plateau."
